{"id":"01adc216b4fceb9d","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-lem-diagonal.md","title":"Diagonal Lemma","display":"lem-diagonal — Diagonal Lemma","type":"lemma","metadata":{"type":"lemma","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-lem-diagonal","aliases":["58-lem-diagonal"],"display":"lem-diagonal — Diagonal Lemma","depends_on":["[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-free-variable]]","[[58-df-substitution-formula]]","[[58-df-godel-numbering]]","[[58-df-derivable]]","[[58-df-theory]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"lemma"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-lem-diagonal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-lem-diagonal</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"lem-diagonal — Diagonal Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"60d957ce43061cb6\" href=\"?note=60d957ce43061cb6\" title=\"58-df-substitution-formula\">58-df-substitution-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"a2b0a7eb56fecb6a\" href=\"?note=a2b0a7eb56fecb6a\" title=\"58-df-godel-numbering\">58-df-godel-numbering</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c470f913608b6d60\" href=\"?note=c470f913608b6d60\" title=\"58-df-derivable\">58-df-derivable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"58-df-theory\">58-df-theory</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,\\varphi,\\psi\\in V\">\\(T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,\\varphi,\\psi\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_0,v_1\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\">\\(v_0,v_1\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (language-indexed theory predicate; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"58-df-theory\">58-df-theory</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma)\\)</span> (formula and term sets).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma\">\\(\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{VarTerm}_\\Sigma\">\\(\\operatorname{VarTerm}_\\Sigma\\)</span> (free-variable operators; see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"715a32e91161b34f\" href=\"?note=715a32e91161b34f\" title=\"58-df-free-variable\">58-df-free-variable</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\">\\(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\)</span> (capture-avoiding formula substitution).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GodelNumbering}_S(g,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{GodelNumbering}_S(g,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (Gödel-numbering predicate).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\)</span> (typed function and derivability predicates).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> (strong diagonal-function representability predicate defined here; the two distinguished variables are explicit arguments).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}represents\\text{-}diagonalization} \\vdash \\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S(T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,v_0,v_1)\\leftrightarrow v_0,v_1\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\land v_0\\neq v_1\\land\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{GodelNumbering}_S(g,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{num},\\omega,\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma))\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{VarTerm}_\\Sigma(\\operatorname{num}(n))=\\emptyset\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(d,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\delta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\delta)\\subseteq\\{v_0,v_1\\}\\land\\forall\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\theta)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\\to d(g(\\theta))=g\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\theta,\\operatorname{num}(g(\\theta)),v_0)\\right)\\Bigr)\\land\\forall n,m\\in\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\\bigl(d(n)=m\\to\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\delta,\\operatorname{num}(n),v_0),\\operatorname{num}(m),v_1\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\bigr)\\land\\bigl(d(n)\\neq m\\to\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\neg\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\delta,\\operatorname{num}(n),v_0),\\operatorname{num}(m),v_1\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}represents\\text{-}diagonalization} \\vdash \\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S(T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,v_0,v_1)\\leftrightarrow v_0,v_1\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\land v_0\\neq v_1\\land\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{GodelNumbering}_S(g,\\Sigma)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{num},\\omega,\\mathrm{Trm}_S(\\Sigma))\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{VarTerm}_\\Sigma(\\operatorname{num}(n))=\\emptyset\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(d,\\omega,\\omega)\\land\\delta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\delta)\\subseteq\\{v_0,v_1\\}\\land\\forall\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\theta)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\\to d(g(\\theta))=g\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\theta,\\operatorname{num}(g(\\theta)),v_0)\\right)\\Bigr)\\land\\forall n,m\\in\\omega\\;\\Bigl(\\bigl(d(n)=m\\to\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\delta,\\operatorname{num}(n),v_0),\\operatorname{num}(m),v_1\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\bigr)\\land\\bigl(d(n)\\neq m\\to\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\neg\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma(\\delta,\\operatorname{num}(n),v_0),\\operatorname{num}(m),v_1\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}diagonal} \\vdash \\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S(T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,v_0,v_1)\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\\to\\exists\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\psi)=\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\psi\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\varphi,\\operatorname{num}(g(\\psi)),v_0\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}diagonal} \\vdash \\mathrm{RepresentsDiagonalization}_S(T,\\Sigma,g,\\operatorname{num},d,\\delta,v_0,v_1)\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\varphi)\\subseteq\\{v_0\\}\\to\\exists\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\;\\Bigl(\\operatorname{FV}_\\Sigma(\\psi)=\\emptyset\\land\\mathrm{Derivable}_S\\!\\left(T,\\psi\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SubFml}_\\Sigma\\!\\left(\\varphi,\\operatorname{num}(g(\\psi)),v_0\\right),\\Sigma\\right)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The diagonal lemma enables self-reference in formal systems and underlies Gödel's incompleteness theorems and Tarski's undefinability theorem.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{num}\">\\(\\operatorname{num}\\)</span> is a designated closed-numeral map, while <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span> sends the code of a one-variable formula to the code of its self-substitution instance.</li>\n<li>The two distinct variables used to represent the graph of diagonalization are part of the predicate signature rather than hidden free parameters.</li>\n<li>The first assertion expands “represents diagonalization” into strong representability by the two-variable formula <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span>; the lemma therefore does not silently assume that every first-order theory can internalize its coding operations.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-free-variable","status":"resolved","id":"715a32e91161b34f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-free-variable]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-substitution-formula","status":"resolved","id":"60d957ce43061cb6","anchor":